-cs.tryShruti
-to.tryShruti
-se.tryShruti


// This is the sequence of 'shrutis' explained in https://bolprocessor.org/two-vina-experiment/
// Here with a 'pramana shruti' = syntonic comma = 81/80 = 21 cents

ORD

gram#1[2] S --> _scale(grama,sa_4) {9 Full_scale _ _ _ , Drone} - _tempo(3/4) _volume(80) {_retro _ Full_scale}
gram#1[3] Full_scale --> sa_4 r1_4 r2_4 r3_4 r4_4 g1_4 g2_4 g3_4 g4_4 m1_4 m2_4 m3p1_4 m4p2_4 p3_4 p4_4 d1_4 d2_4 d3_4 d4_4 n1_4 n2_4 n3_4 n4_4 sa_5
gram#1[4] Drone --> _volume(30) Droneseq Droneseq Droneseq Droneseq Droneseq Droneseq Droneseq Droneseq
gram#1[5] Droneseq --> {_legato(300) p4_3 sa_4 sa_4 sa_3}


// Technical note: In MIDI, we use different channels to apply pitch bend to individual notes. The volume(30) setting contradicts the default volume(60) setting for notes in the scale, thereby creating unwanted noise when notes in the drone are extinguished. To avoid this, the machine automatically converts volume() to velocity when the microtonal (MPE) approach is used.